#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0460 expect=violation domain=AE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the High Level Term (--HLT) is not on the MedDRA primary system organ class hierarchy path.
#note "EC-36 pin: the rule's dictionary_parent is the template --SOC. Until EC-36 the retired operation evaluator copied it verbatim, looked up a column literally named '--SOC', missed, and returned null — the rule reported EXECUTED with 0 findings, a false 'checked and clean'. Since wave 1 of the operation→function programme dictionary_parent is a typed column parameter of valid_external_dictionary_hierarchy, resolved to AESOC by the shared parameter path (the hand-written arm is unrepresentable). Row 1's HLT 'Headaches NEC' sits under 'Nervous system disorders', so the 'Gastrointestinal disorders' SOC is off-path and must fire. Both operands carry the MedDRA preferred case, so the miss is the hierarchy path itself and not a case mismatch (C1 repair)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col AEHLT type=Char label="High Level Term"
col AESOC type=Char label="Primary System Organ Class"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | Headaches NEC | Gastrointestinal disorders
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 2 | Headaches NEC | Nervous system disorders
---
